For every index i that thread zero reads, 0 ≤ i < valid ≤ 96, so thread i exists and writes entries[i] before reaching the barrier. Every thread reaches that same unconditional barrier, which makes those writes visible to thread zero before its summation. Entries at indices valid through 95 may remain uninitialized, but are never read. Summing at most 96 integer inputs in a long long avoids integer overflow on CUDA's 32-bit int and 64-bit long long types.

